  "notes": "SOURCE OF TRUTH: the developer's own Dropbox share (link in developerCloudUrl), one folder\nper project with Photos / Presentation / Price list. The price lists are real per-unit tables\nwith SOLD and RESERVED markers, so this developer gets real units — unlike Marinakis.\n\nSCOPE RULED BY THE OPERATOR 2026-10-29: only the projects that have a Dropbox sale folder.\nThat is seven folders. The Q4 2026 deck lists sixteen projects; Forum, Romana A+B, Vesta,\nRiva, Rodi, Guru Mountain Resort, Amathus Heights, Liberty and Atlantida Court C have no sale\nfolder and are NOT imported. The FOR RENT folder (Atlantida Court C apt 101/102, ONLY Tower\napt 701) is out of scope — we sell, we do not let.\nLEVEL holds two products: Level Residences (houses) and Level Plots (building land, own price\nlist and own presentation). The operator ruled the PLOTS OUT 2026-10-29: our property-type\nfilter knows no 'plot' and the project page is built around bedrooms and covered area.\nThe five near-sold-out projects (iHome, ONLY, Level, Luma, Alti) are all IN, by the same ruling.\n\nWHERE SOURCES DISAGREE THE PRICE LIST WINS (same rule as Marinakis):\n - Mandarin delivery: deck says January 2029, price list says May 2029 -> May 2029.\n - iHome: the deck advertises the available stock as 'Duplex 3 Bedroom with a Roof Garden';\n   the price list calls A101/A701 plain apartments and shows no roof-garden column. We carry\n   apartments and claim no roof garden. OPEN QUESTION for the developer.\n - Luma location: the price list says 'Agia Varvara, Limassol'; the pin in the presentation\n   (34.715813, 33.149176) reverse-geocodes to Agios Tychonas, 1.3 km from Alti. Agia Varvara\n   is a micro-locality inside Agios Tychonas, so area = Agios Tychonas (our existing label,\n   8 published projects) and the text may name Agia Varvara as the spot.\n - ONLY Tower: the price list says 'Germasogeia'; the company's own letterhead puts the\n   building at Potamos Germasogeias 4046 and the pin confirms the coast road -> area =\n   Potamos Germasogeias.\n\nPINS: taken from the !3d/!4d pair or the degree string of the Maps links in the PDFs, never\nfrom the @lat,lng camera part (see the map-pin @-fallback trap). All seven reverse-geocode to\nthe area we store.\n\nPRICE LIST DATES differ a lot: Mandarin and Athina 23/10/2026, ONLY 26/10/2026, Level\n29/09/2026, Luma 19/03/2026, iHome 05/06/2025 (sixteen months old). Alti has NO price list at\nall; its single unit comes from the House 2 presentation and the Q4 deck.\n\nVAT: all prices are net '+ VAT' EXCEPT iHome's two units, which the list marks 'VAT PAID'.\n\nEXTRAS worth a button once we have the feature: 360 tours dtagroup.com/360/level/ and\ndtagroup.com/360/luma/, project video youtube.com/watch?v=S774eoakAmE (iHome).\n\nClient registration: not yet done — no partner/agent portal found on dtagroup.com."
